BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:28c7b71dd4d93bfa3efa8e25fb7e14b8@events.appsterdam.rs
SUMMARY:Coffee Coding
DESCRIPTION:Whether you are a seasoned programmer or learning to code Apps, wouldn’t it be cool to run by your challenge with another programmer when you get stuck? Or you have questions, or simply want to be in the environment of other like-minded friends while you work on your project?\n\nWelcome to Appsterdam.\n\nBring your laptop and get feedback, encouragement and support, no matter what level you are at.\n\nShare and contribute. Get guidance. Feel good.\n\nAll levels are welcome, so don’t be shy.\n\nIn the future we plan to have break-out sessions where we will have short talks on valuable topics and also conduct mini-hackathons where all of us get to participate and learn together.\n\nMaike and Daniel are super committed to have an inspired group.\n\nWe start at 9:30 and end at 11:30 sharp, so some a bit closer to 9:30 to make sure you get the help you desire.\n\nJust ask and maybe we can help you with:\n\n• Android Development\n\n• iOS Development\n\n• Flutter Development\n\n• C++\n\n• JavaScript\n\n• Python\n\n• Rust\n\n• UX/UI Design (Adobe XD, Balsamiq, Keynote, Sketch, Figma)
DTSTART:20260905T093000
DTEND:20260905T113000
LOCATION:Kinkerstraat 110, Amsterdam
CLASS:PUBLIC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
ORGANIZER;CN="Dániel Varga":MAILTO:Dániel@appsterdam.rs
ATTENDEE;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;RSVP=TRUE;CN="Dániel Varga":MAILTO:Dániel@appsterdam.rs
ATTENDEE;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;RSVP=TRUE;CN="Maike Warner":MAILTO:Maike@appsterdam.rs
CATEGORIES:Appsterdam Events
URL:https://meetup.com/appsterdam/events/316137501
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f4dfdd9234717979301ec4b924d981d9@events.appsterdam.rs
SUMMARY:🥪 Lunch & Launch 🚀 
DESCRIPTION:What happens when makers, sensor builders and data enthusiasts share a terrain? Tom van Arman and the Marineterrein community are about to show you. Over the last several months we have centralized live data from 12 sensors on the Marineterrein Amsterdam into two new tools: an operational dashboard for the property managers, and public infoscreens for visitors at every entrance. Together they cover sound, crowd flow, busy locations, vehicle types, and water and air temperature - a first real-time picture of livability and resilience on the Marineterrein.\n\nAt this 🥪**Lunch & Launch**🚀, you'll meet the people who built it. Five members of our sensing community will present their own sensors and discuss how the data is helping improve accessibility and resilience on the Marineterrein, today and in the future:\n\n**Ilias Jelasity** & **Emilie Taffouraud** \- Computational Social Science Capstone Students from UvA will unveil the new public dashboard and its many features and functionalities\.\n\n**[Michiel Bontenbal](https://www.linkedin.com/in/michielbontenbal/)** - Digital Media & Creative Industry Lecturer at the HvA - demos the Urban Sound Sensor and what it reveals about livability on the terrain.\n\n**[Michael de By](https://www.linkedin.com/in/michaeldeby/)** - CEO & Founder of Husense - presents privacy-proof monitoring, and how sensing can respect the people it observes.\n\n**[Martin Frissen](https://www.linkedin.com/in/martin-frissen/)** - Amsterdam Sensemakers and technical advisor for HvA's HBO-ICT programme "Studio Smart Cities" - shares his perspective on sensemaking in the city.\n\n**[Laura Ponoran](https://www.linkedin.com/in/laura-ponoran/)** - AI, Data & Smart City Research Assistant at Tapp - presents the Busyness Monitor and demos the public web app she built on top of it.\n\nExpect short, hands-on demos rather than slide decks, plenty of room for technical questions, and a chance to compare notes with others building sensing projects of their own. Whether you're a student, researcher, or fellow sensor-builder, this is your invitation to see what's under the hood - and to help shape where the Marineterrein's sensing network goes next.
DTSTART:20260909T120000
DTEND:20260909T130000
LOCATION:Kattenburgerstraat 5, Commandantswoning, Amsterdam
CLASS:PUBLIC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
ORGANIZER;CN="Tom van Arman":MAILTO:Tom@appsterdam.rs
ATTENDEE;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;RSVP=TRUE;CN="Tom van Arman":MAILTO:Tom@appsterdam.rs
